    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/05/brooks-glycerin-22-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: DNA Tuned creates a plush, softer heel with solid impact protection for daily and long runs, while the forefoot feels slightly firmer.",
        "Responsiveness: The smaller-cell forefoot foam adds a noticeably snappier toe-off than prior versions, but overall energy return is still not high enough for true fast-effort use.",
        "Stability: Despite being neutral, it rides stable from a wide flared platform and strong lockdown; the heel counter is very stiff and supportive, while sidewall guidance is mild.",
        "Durability: Durability is characterized as average, with outsole grip reported as good in most situations and no major material longevity problems specifically called out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/brooks-glycerin-22-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The DNA Tuned midsole delivers a soft heel landing, strong impact protection, and a smooth heel-to-forefoot transition; overall underfoot comfort is high.",
        "Responsiveness: The forefoot tuning creates a responsive, sometimes snappy toe-off with noticeable bounce for a daily trainer.",
        "Stability: Despite the high stack, the firmer carrier foam keeps the ride stable, and heel lockdown is good; torsional rigidity/lateral structure are not deeply detailed.",
        "Durability: Outsole durability is a standout, with lots of forefoot rubber and repeated claims of rock-solid longevity and long outdoor life."
      ]
    }
